    "turn_text": "my uncle was a teacher so yeah we've got teachers in our family and look it's a very tough job and you know we should have the most respect for them and try to help try to help these teachers and God bless them they're making a difference I mean if you think back and you know everybody thinks back in their life and their teachers you know if we're lucky we've had some teachers that have really made a difference in our lives I mean just made a big difference and so that's what that's what teachers can do so it is as you say it's a balance that we're trying to strike School choice was not intended to be there for families, frankly, who could afford to make that choice. It's for families who can't afford to make that choice, to try to put them in the same position as more fluent families. When they're in a position that their public school was not good. And that was the original intent. I think the intent is correct. And what I hope the legislature does, I set up a meeting with the Speaker and the Senate President that's going to occur in the next few days. And I'm going to just say, look, we need to move this thing forward. We need to get a resolution to this impasse. There's an impasse between the House and the Senate. We've got to get this. And we also have to be able to do this because we want to be able to tell people what the rules are, what the deal is. We just can't let this linger on any longer.",
