  {
    "episode_id": 71773,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71773.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 72,
    "turn_text": "Well, bureaucracy can get in the way of getting results. I don't think there's any doubt about that. We are a state that is a local government state. Most of our services are delivered locally. My job as governor is to try to be a good partner with the local communities. the local townships, villages, cities, and counties. In the school area, we have 630-some school districts, and they're locally run by elected, generally by elected school boards. And I think that is good. I think occasionally you will see situations where there's too much bureaucracy, and I think we always have to be vigilant about that and make sure that The focus is on kids. As we have these debates, I guess my only plea really to everybody who's engaging in this debate about school choice and public schools is let's remember that our focus has to be entirely on the kids. That's what this is about in making sure kids, you know, have the opportunity to live up to their full potential. I mean, if we look at the future of Ohio, I look at where are we going as a state? I'm",
