    "turn_text": "took the lead he's he's the one that did it he and his men and women uh... you know they had the idea that It's something that would never have been thought of 10 years ago. And that is that the sheriff law enforcement would be involved with getting people into treatment. I mean, no one ever thought that that's, you know, it's not classically the law enforcement's job, but what he saw was that people were going to hospitals. They were taking their overdose, taking their in the emergency. And then once they got better, they just two hours, three hours, four hours later, they just walked out and nothing happened. And he said, you know, Hey, this should be maybe a teachable moment. Maybe that maybe this is the opportunity for that individual. And they've been maybe they're scared to death. Maybe something the family who's responded is now scared to death. And they say, this is maybe an opportunity to get that person into treatment. So they send out a deputy and the deputy's job is to talk to that person and say, hey, you want to go into treatment? If you do, we're going to work with you and we're going to get you into treatment. That was revolutionary. And you know, it's being done. Right here. And modeled around other parts of the",
