    "turn_idx": 116,
    "turn_text": "We are. There is one and Dr. Amy Acton who I appointed to be the head of the Department of Health has really taken a proactive role and I want to really give a shout out to Lucas County Health Department and every health department in northwest Ohio because they are focused on this. And if you are in a situation where, you know, you think that there's a possibility that someone you or someone in your family has come from China and that you maybe have this problem, you know, we need you to contact the county health department where you live. because they're directly tied into us in Columbus, and we're going to monitor this. I think one of the things that I want to point out, and Dr. Acton and I were talking about this on the phone as I was driving to Toledo, last year in the United States we lost 35,000 people who died of the flu. Just the",
